A||N||9||Monkeyman||Quick stereo question||||5||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||12-02-2000||06:04 PM||||I just bought a nice Sony CD headunit.  It has a separate output (RCA) for a sub.  I bought Oreifs powered Bazooka tube, too.  I can't run the sub through an amp ('cause it's already powered?) and there don't seem to be any RCA jacks on the sub/tube.<P>How can I make this work?  Do I need to buy a non-powered Bazooka tube and an amp?  Seems like a waste of money when I have a sub/tube already.  I'd like to use the sub out on the stereo because of some of the features built into the stereo.<P>Eventually, I'll probably buy some (1?) real subs and an amp to run them, but that's in the distant future.  (Costs money)||||reg||5
Z||000001||RNGCRSH||12-02-2000||06:12 PM||||Just make a patch cable with RCA on one end and speaker wire in the other end. the center of the RCA is + the outer is -. This should work. there should be enough signal to drive the amp.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||12-02-2000||06:28 PM||||Monkeyman, Just run the RCA from the stereo to the  Bazooka tube. There is an RCA connection as part of the harness that plugs into the tube. That's how I had it hooked up in my car.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 12-02-2000).]||||reg||4
Z||000003||Monkeyman||12-02-2000||06:28 PM||||So I could just cut the end off of an RCA cable?  Is there a wire inside a wire?  (Now I just have to find the wiring harness for the Bazooka tube. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||12-02-2000||06:31 PM||||Looks like we posted at the same time, Oreif. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Turns out the only problem I have now is finding the harness (I've just gotta clean up my computer/bed/junk/car parts room. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)||||reg||1
