Z||000006||Monkeyman||12-02-2000||06:39 PM||||I've got the harness somewhere.  I wasn't trying to accuse you of not sending it.  Just that I can't seem to find it now. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||KRMFiero||12-02-2000||08:16 PM||||Hmm I'm not sure If i would do that, before I had a Head unit that just had regular speaker outputs, I splised a RCA and pluged the RCA end into my amp and hooked the spliced end to the headunit, 2 days later the amp was junk..... of course this is the opposite in your case and you will be feeding a low voltage signal to something (from what it sounds like) that is ment to take alot of volts/watts     well i think you get what i mean, good luck||||reg||1
Z||000008||overlord||12-02-2000||11:19 PM||||if the bass tube has an amp built in with it...wouldnt you need to hook it up to a power sourcer (12v)? and ground.<P>If it is  the same as the bass tubes i used to have then you just hook it up to a + and - leads from a speaker ouput. Then run  one wire to the battery and ground the thing.<P>just incase.....you are having  problems still||||reg||1
Z||000009||Monkeyman||12-02-2000||11:24 PM||||Oreif said that the wiring harness has RCA plugs.  I also need to hook up power and ground leads.  I'll be set once I figure out what I did with the harness.||||reg||1
